        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cave_spring_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The landscape around Cave Spring is hilly and mostly forested, with elevations reaching up to 1,200 feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_Spring%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sallisaw Creek, a tributary of the Arkansas River, forms the southeastern boundary of Cave Spring.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_Spring%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Geological formations in the Cave Spring area once provided essential protection and water for early Cherokee settlements.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cave_spring_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Railroads like the Kansas City Southern linked Cave Spring to the county seat of Stilwell by the late nineteenth century.",
